  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (combo): Everything at once. mild: aged paper, bleed-through, a few pencil marks, 3 deg skew, JPEG 60. scan: phone photo (250 dpi) of an aged, stained, pencil-marked page with hand shadow, JPEG 50. severe: 150 dpi book scan with curl + gutter, -7 deg skew, foxing, 25% bleed-through, stain, pencil + ballpoint marks, punch holes, motion blur, noise and JPEG 25 - a worst case. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Handwritten marks, stains, foxing and ghost notes are not music and are not in the truth. Severe is intentionally at (or beyond) the limit of human legibility at 150 dpi."
 },
